CPZ UI
======

Menu and tabs
-------------
  Alt+O          Open Apps Manager
  Alt+H          Help
  Alt+T          New tab (Home)
  Alt+W          Close the current tab
  Alt+R          Rename the current tab
  Alt+L          List open tabs
  Alt+Tab        Next tab
  Alt+Shift+Tab  Previous tab
  Alt+1..9       Select tab

System apps
-----------
  F/X/Z/C        Move; Enter opens or applies; Esc goes back
  Esc            Exits the app at its top level

Panes
-----
  Alt+V          Split left/right
  Alt+B          Split top/bottom
  Alt+N          Next pane
  Alt+P          Previous pane
  Alt+Z          Zoom / unzoom pane
  Alt+X          Close pane

Copy and paste
--------------
  Alt+C          Enter copy mode
  Alt+Y          Paste the tmux buffer
  In copy mode:  j/k move, Ctrl+U/D or Fn+L/M page,
                 Space selects, Enter copies, q exits.

Terminal
--------
  Ctrl+Shift+C   Copy selection
  Ctrl+Shift+V   Paste
  Shift+PageUp   Scroll back
  Shift+PageDown Scroll forward

Language
--------
  Alt+Space      Switch keyboard layout (us, ua)

Session
-------
  There is one tmux session. Session switching, renaming and creation are
  disabled. C-a is the advanced tmux prefix fallback; daily actions use Alt.
  The tmux server survives a compositor restart, a terminal restart and an
  output switch. A new tab starts Home; choosing an app replaces the tab.
  Closing the last tab recreates a Home tab instead of taking the UI down.

  Recovery is available over the serial console and SSH.
